            {
              "text": "With NO<sub>2</sub> in large excess, [NO<sub>2</sub>] hardly changes, so <i>k</i>[NO<sub>2</sub>] acts as one constant, <i>k</i>'. The reaction is then pseudo-first order, and for any first-order reaction <i>t</i><sub>½</sub> = ln 2 / <i>k</i> = 0.693 / <i>k</i>, independent of the starting concentration. So <i>t</i><sub>½</sub> = 0.693 / 0.0101 = 68.6 s. The initial [F<sub>2</sub>] of 4.00 × 10<sup>–5</sup> mol dm<sup>–3</sup> is not needed.",
